import Lean
open Lean Elab

/-!
A long-lived Lean process for the stage-0 lanes: it imports Mathlib once and then serves
requests.  Each request is elaborated from the same immutable imported `Environment`, but the
process is NOT isolated between requests: process-global state (`IO.Ref`s, extension caches such
as the `exact?` lazy discrimination tree, `initialize`d refs) persists.  Callers must not rely on
isolation between requests; see `automation_portfolio.WarmWorker` for how the lanes cope with it.

Protocol (one request per stdin line, every reply ends with `PALS_DONE <path>`):
* `<path>`            elaborate the command file at `<path>`, print every message;
* `CHECK <path>`      statement check, parse only (the statement is never elaborated): line 1 of
                      the file is the opened namespaces, line 2 the term.  Prints
                      `PALS_CHECK_OK` or `PALS_CHECK_REFUSED <reason>`;
* `KINDS <path>`      print the syntax node kinds of the term (used to curate the allow-list).
-/

/-- Syntax node kinds a proposition may contain (parse level).  Everything else is refused.
Excluded on purpose: `by`, `show`, `from`, `let`, `have`, `do`, `match`, quotations, anonymous
constructors, `·`, structure instances, term-position elaborators (`type_of%`, `binop%`, `by_elab`,
`%[ ]`, ...), attributes and every command. -/
-- BEGIN ALLOWED_KINDS (generated by scripts/eval/gen_allowed_kinds.py, reviewed by hand)
